WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.260
Accessibility should shape media production from the beginning.

2
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:16.813
Readable contrast, plain language, alt text planning, captions, transcripts, and keyboard and screen-reader considerations all affect whether learners can access and understand the course.

3
00:00:16.813 --> 00:00:24.954
Accessibility also improves the experience for learners on small screens, in noisy environments, or under time constraints.

4
00:00:24.954 --> 00:00:29.747
Alt text should describe the instructional purpose of meaningful images.

5
00:00:29.747 --> 00:00:37.735
Decorative images may not need detailed descriptions, but diagrams, screenshots, charts, and process visuals usually do.

6
00:00:37.735 --> 00:00:41.995
Captions and transcripts should be available for audio and video.

7
00:00:41.995 --> 00:00:48.766
Plain language helps learners focus on the concept rather than decoding unnecessarily complex writing.

8
00:00:48.766 --> 00:00:52.342
File size and performance are production concerns too.

9
00:00:52.342 --> 00:00:59.113
Oversized images, heavy videos, and unnecessary effects can slow course loading or frustrate learners.

10
00:00:59.113 --> 00:01:02.917
Export settings should balance quality with performance.

11
00:01:02.917 --> 00:01:11.818
A beautiful asset that makes a module sluggish may harm the learning experience, especially for remote learners or constrained networks.

12
00:01:11.818 --> 00:01:18.361
Stakeholder review should confirm accuracy, tone, completeness, brand fit, and learner relevance.

13
00:01:18.361 --> 00:01:27.186
Media QA should check readability, audio quality, captions, transcripts, links, visual consistency, file naming, and export quality.

14
00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:36.924
LMS packaging considerations should include launch behavior, tracking requirements, and whether media loads correctly from the published package.

15
00:01:36.924 --> 00:01:40.500
Quality assurance is not a single final click-through.

16
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.097
It is a production habit.

17
00:01:42.097 --> 00:01:44.304
Review scripts before recording.

18
00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:46.206
Check visuals before export.

19
00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:48.108
Confirm captions with audio.

20
00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:50.238
Verify downloadable resources.

21
00:01:50.238 --> 00:01:53.661
Test the course package in the intended environment.

22
00:01:53.661 --> 00:01:59.443
The goal is to ensure assets support learning for more people across devices and contexts.
